                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5933ed36-74b4-3794-860b-a11063c9999a",
                        "entry_id": "2f7e3a97-26b5-32c5-addf-4bc883ce04d0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To study zoology, especially by collecting animals to be studied."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "926f26a0-8c95-4fdc-97f7-bb2b87591db0",
                                "sense_id": "5933ed36-74b4-3794-860b-a11063c9999a",
                                "text": "There it erects tents capable of holding about one hundred and fifty people, and there the members and their friends gather for a fortnight to climb mountains, botanize, zoologize, or merely enjoy life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cc58aee5-f291-4f16-a1a4-a13506ee1e7e",
                                "sense_id": "5933ed36-74b4-3794-860b-a11063c9999a",
                                "text": "She is later joined by CK, who delights in the opportunity to zoologize on the sea-shore."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2ec99ac-b364-4222-8287-1f9e5d9101bf",
                                "sense_id": "5933ed36-74b4-3794-860b-a11063c9999a",
                                "text": "Broaden your horizons beyond the field that you were trained in so that you resist the ever-present temptation to over-engineer, over-botanize, or over-zoologize the wetlands that you create and restore."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "be58d916-1a0f-3a54-8b2e-8c0dbbcafe24",
                        "entry_id": "2f7e3a97-26b5-32c5-addf-4bc883ce04d0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To discuss zoology."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "291ed000-b20a-4b67-af35-4203ccb122b3",
                                "sense_id": "be58d916-1a0f-3a54-8b2e-8c0dbbcafe24",
                                "text": "The only compensation he could get seems to have been to botanize and zoologize, as it were, on his visitors."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52fcd1d9-38e4-418e-9d19-3e985c93d637",
                                "sense_id": "be58d916-1a0f-3a54-8b2e-8c0dbbcafe24",
                                "text": "Somehow, wherever Sue was, Ned always seemed in the same vicinity, discussing fiddler crabs or something equally slimy, and they seem likely to zoologize through life together."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
